  "verses": [
    {"number":1,"sourceRef":"eng-web:ZEC:14:1","text":"Look, the day of the LORD is coming, when your plunder will be divided right among you."},
    {"number":2,"sourceRef":"eng-web:ZEC:14:2","text":"“I’ll gather all nations to fight Jerusalem. The city will be captured, its houses looted, and its women raped. Half the city will go into exile, but the rest of the people won’t be taken away from the city."},
    {"number":3,"sourceRef":"eng-web:ZEC:14:3","text":"Then the LORD will go out and fight those nations, as he has fought in battles before."},
    {"number":4,"sourceRef":"eng-web:ZEC:14:4","text":"On that day his feet will stand on the Mount of Olives, east of Jerusalem. The mountain will split in two from east to west, forming a huge valley. Half the mountain will shift north, and half south."},
    {"number":5,"sourceRef":"eng-web:ZEC:14:5","text":"You’ll flee through the valley between my mountains, because it will reach as far as Azel. You’ll flee just as people fled the earthquake in the days of Uzziah, king of Judah. Then the LORD my God will come, and all the holy ones with him."},
    {"number":6,"sourceRef":"eng-web:ZEC:14:6","text":"On that day there will be no light, no cold, and no frost."},
    {"number":7,"sourceRef":"eng-web:ZEC:14:7","text":"It will be a day unlike any other, known only to the LORD—not day and not night. Yet when evening comes, there will be light."},
    {"number":8,"sourceRef":"eng-web:ZEC:14:8","text":"On that day fresh water will flow out of Jerusalem, half toward the eastern sea and half toward the western sea. It will keep flowing in summer and winter."},
    {"number":9,"sourceRef":"eng-web:ZEC:14:9","text":"The LORD will be King over the whole earth…176 tokens truncated…t while they’re still standing, their eyes will rot in their sockets, and their tongues will rot in their mouths."},
    {"number":13,"sourceRef":"eng-web:ZEC:14:13","text":"On that day the LORD will send a great panic among them. Each person will grab the hand of someone nearby, and they’ll turn against one another."},
    {"number":14,"sourceRef":"eng-web:ZEC:14:14","text":"Judah will also fight at Jerusalem. The wealth of the surrounding nations—gold, silver, and clothing in great abundance—will be gathered there."},
    {"number":15,"sourceRef":"eng-web:ZEC:14:15","text":"A plague like this will also strike the horses, mules, camels, donkeys, and every animal in those camps."},
    {"number":16,"sourceRef":"eng-web:ZEC:14:16","text":"Everyone left from the nations that attacked Jerusalem will go up each year to worship the King, the LORD of Armies, and celebrate the Festival of Shelters."},
    {"number":17,"sourceRef":"eng-web:ZEC:14:17","text":"If any family on earth refuses to go up to Jerusalem to worship the King, the LORD of Armies, it won’t get rain."},
    {"number":18,"sourceRef":"eng-web:ZEC:14:18","text":"If Egypt’s family refuses to go up, it won’t get rain either. The LORD will strike with this plague every nation that refuses to celebrate the Festival of Shelters."},
    {"number":19,"sourceRef":"eng-web:ZEC:14:19","text":"That will be the punishment for Egypt and every nation that refuses to go up and celebrate the Festival of Shelters."},
    {"number":20,"sourceRef":"eng-web:ZEC:14:20","text":"On that day the words “HOLY TO THE LORD” will be engraved on the bells of the horses. The cooking pots in the LORD’s house will be like the bowls before the altar."},
    {"number":21,"sourceRef":"eng-web:ZEC:14:21","text":"Every pot in Jerusalem and Judah will be holy to the LORD of Armies. Everyone who offers a sacrifice will come and use them to cook. On that day no Canaanite will remain in the house of the LORD of Armies."}
  ]
}

